WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.509
Ever tried to sit still, only to have

2
00:00:01.509 --> 00:00:03.297
your mind wander seconds later?

3
00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:06.928
A disciple asks: Why does my mind wander

4
00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:11.270
in meditation? The Jagadguru offers a question.

5
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.917
Count your entire month's salary in rupee

6
00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:17.005
notes, without a single error. Would your

7
00:00:17.005 --> 00:00:20.697
mind wander? No. The count matters too

8
00:00:20.697 --> 00:00:24.726
much. Then consider: is it capacity you

9
00:00:24.726 --> 00:00:27.651
lack, or the importance you give the practice?

10
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:30.365
An elephant's trunk reaches for everything

11
00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:32.652
in the market. Give it a bamboo stick to

12
00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:35.926
hold. The mind, too, needs a support: a

13
00:00:35.926 --> 00:00:39.571
mantra, the breath, a chosen practice.

14
00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:41.197
Something to return to.

15
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:44.723
When attention wanders, notice the rhythm.

16
00:00:44.723 --> 00:00:47.417
Return gently to the anchor. In the game,

17
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:50.342
tap with the beat. In practice, return

18
00:00:50.342 --> 00:00:51.991
to the breath or mantra.

19
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:54.594
Then make a ten-minute contract. Put the

20
00:00:54.594 --> 00:00:56.719
email, deadlines, and worries on a shelf.

21
00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:57.636
They can wait.

22
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.088
Walk through seven temple gates, from

23
00:01:00.088 --> 00:01:02.340
the noisy bazaar toward the quiet within.

24
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.264
As attention becomes steadier, the guides

25
00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.528
grow quieter. The training wheels fall

26
00:01:07.528 --> 00:01:10.268
away, and the inward journey continues.

27
00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:12.845
The supports fall away. Attention remains.

28
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.310
The Srirangam Corridor. Inspired by chapters

29
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.783
eight and nine of The Self-Driving Mind.

30
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:21.685
Read the idea. Experience the metaphor.

31
00:01:21.685 --> 00:01:23.206
Take the four-minute walk.